[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Starlark for .NET - language and library
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Draft, Active, Implemented, Open)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[FREETEXT]
What the lexer, parser, interpreter, type system and static checker shall do. The normative source is the Starlark
language specification (starlark-spec/spec.md). Where this implementation chooses differently, the choice is recorded
in docs/DEVIATIONS.md.
[/FREETEXT]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Lexing and parsing

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-SYN-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Lexical grammar
STATEMENT: >>>
The lexer shall tokenize identifiers, keywords, integer literals (decimal, hexadecimal, octal and binary), float
literals, string and bytes literals (single, double, triple-quoted, raw and escaped), operators and comments, and shall
produce Indent and Dedent tokens from line indentation as Python does.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Syntax.Tests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-SYN-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Indentation errors
STATEMENT: >>>
The lexer shall reject tabs in indentation, inconsistent dedent, and unterminated strings with an error that carries
the source span.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Syntax.Tests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-SYN-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Parser
STATEMENT: >>>
The parser shall build an abstract syntax tree for the whole Starlark grammar (statements, expressions, comprehensions,
lambdas, slices, f-strings and type annotations when enabled) with correct operator precedence and with spans for
every node.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Syntax.Tests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-SYN-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Dialect switches
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional syntax (top-level statements, f-strings, type annotations, positional-only and keyword-only parameters) shall
be accepted only when its dialect flag is enabled, and rejected with a clear error otherwise.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Syntax.Tests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-SYN-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Termination on any input
STATEMENT: >>>
The lexer and parser shall terminate and either succeed or report an error for every input, including unterminated
f-strings and random byte sequences.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Fuzz.Tests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-SYN-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Error message parity
STATEMENT: >>>
Syntax errors shall match the messages and positions of the reference starlark-rust golden files.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Syntax.Tests (Goldens)

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Values and operators

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-VAL-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Data types
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall provide NoneType, bool, int (arbitrary precision), float (IEEE 754 double), string, bytes, list,
tuple, dict (insertion ordered), set, range and function values with the semantics of the specification.
<<<
VERIFICATION: EvalTests, ConformanceTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-VAL-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Arithmetic
STATEMENT: >>>
Integer arithmetic shall be exact, with floored division and modulo; float arithmetic shall follow IEEE 754; mixed
int and float operations and comparisons shall be exact; int to float conversion shall round to nearest, ties to even.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (04-10), GoSuiteTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-VAL-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Equality, ordering and hashing
STATEMENT: >>>
Equality, ordering and hashing shall follow the specification: only hashable values are dict keys and set elements,
int and float keys that are equal collide, and ordering of unorderable types is an error.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (34-35, 56), GoSuiteTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-VAL-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Freezing and mutation
STATEMENT: >>>
Global values shall be frozen after a module finishes; mutating a frozen value, or a collection while it is being
iterated, shall be an error.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ConformanceTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-VAL-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: String element size
STATEMENT: >>>
String length, indexing and slicing shall use UTF-16 code units by default and UTF-8 bytes when selected by the host.
A separate utf16 type shall be available as an extension.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Utf16TypeTests, StringElements tests

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Statements and functions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-EXE-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Statements
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall execute assignment (including unpacking and augmented forms), if, for, break, continue, pass,
return, def, lambda, load and expression statements.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-EXE-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Scoping
STATEMENT: >>>
Name resolution shall be static with local, enclosing, global, predeclared and universal scopes. A global may not be
rebound unless the host allows it, and a local used before assignment shall be an error.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (41-45)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-EXE-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Calls
STATEMENT: >>>
Calls shall support positional, named, default, *args and **kwargs parameters, with the specified errors for missing,
duplicate and unexpected arguments. Recursion shall be rejected.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (46-50)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-EXE-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Comprehensions
STATEMENT: >>>
List and dict comprehensions, including nested for and if clauses, shall execute with their own scope.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (30, 37)

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Built-in functions and methods

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-LIB-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Built-in functions
STATEMENT: >>>
All built-in functions of the specification shall be provided (abs, all, any, bool, bytes, dict, dir, enumerate, fail,
float, getattr, hasattr, hash, int, len, list, max, min, print, range, repr, reversed, set, sorted, str, tuple, type,
zip) with the specified argument and error behaviour.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ConformanceTests, ExampleProgramTests (64-70)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-LIB-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: String methods and formatting
STATEMENT: >>>
All string methods of the specification shall be provided, as well as percent formatting and the format method with
the specified conversions and errors.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (11-24)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-LIB-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Container methods
STATEMENT: >>>
The methods of list, dict and set shall be provided with the specified results and errors.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (25-40, 51-56)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-LIB-004
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Bytes methods
STATEMENT: >>>
bytes shall provide the string-like methods of the specification beyond elems, once the specification defines them.
<<<
COMMENT: The specification marks these as TODO; see docs/DEVIATIONS.md.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-LIB-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Conformance suites
STATEMENT: >>>
The implementation shall pass the Bazel, Go, Java and Rust conformance data, including the Go float and set suites,
modulo the wording differences recorded in the harness.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ConformanceTests, GoSuiteTests

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Type system and extensions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-TYP-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Annotations
STATEMENT: >>>
When types are enabled, parameter, return and variable annotations shall be checked at run time against int, str,
bool, float, None, list[T], dict[K, V], tuple forms, unions, typing.Any, typing.Callable and user types, with
messages that name the argument and the expected type.
<<<
VERIFICATION: TypeSystemTests, ExampleProgramTests (71-80)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-TYP-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: isinstance and type values
STATEMENT: >>>
isinstance and eval_type shall accept types as values, including parametrized and union types, and shall reject
non-types.
<<<
VERIFICATION: TypeSystemTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-TYP-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Records, enums and structs
STATEMENT: >>>
record, field, enum and struct shall be provided, with typed fields, defaults, equality, repr, dir, indexing and
iteration of enums, and errors for wrong or missing fields.
<<<
VERIFICATION: ExampleProgramTests (81-86)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-TYP-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: JSON module
STATEMENT: >>>
json.encode, json.decode and json.indent shall round-trip nested data including big integers and string escapes, and
shall reject invalid input and cyclic structures.
<<<
VERIFICATION: JsonTests, ExampleProgramTests (87-90)

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Static checker

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-CHK-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Lenient checking
STATEMENT: >>>
The checker shall report an error only when it can prove two types cannot intersect, and shall never report an error for
a program that runs correctly (no false positives on the conformance corpus).
<<<
VERIFICATION: TypeCheckerTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-CHK-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Struct, record, enum and json types
STATEMENT: >>>
The checker shall know the fields of structs and records, the members of enums, and the signatures of json functions,
and shall report unknown attributes and wrongly typed arguments with the reference wording.
<<<
VERIFICATION: TypeCheckerPrecisionTests

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: LANG-CHK-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Agreement with the runtime
STATEMENT: >>>
A program the checker rejects for a type reason shall also fail at run time, checked by property tests.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Starlark.Fuzz.Tests (PropertyTests)

[/SECTION]
